	order_index: 2
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"In &6Create: Forge Frontier&r the mod &5Apotheosis&r overhauls the vanilla system for enchanting. It does this by introducing some new stats to enchanting tables and new bookshelves to alter those stats."
				""
				"These stats are as follows:"
				"&n&aEterna&r&r (Enchanting Power)"
				"&n&4Quanta&r&r (Enchanting Flux)"
				"&5&nArcana&r&r (Enchanting Rarity)"
				""
				"Other modifiers that can be added are:"
				"&eRectification&r"
				"&3Enchanting Clues&r"
				"&6Treasure Enchantments&r"
			]
			id: "6965F4ABCAB88875"
			rewards: [{
				id: "48F1F245E472FD1F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 200
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 3.0d
			subtitle: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2D29A403707CC3C6"
				item: "minecraft:book"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Introduction to Enchanting"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6965F4ABCAB88875"]
			description: [
				"&5Apotheosis&r changes many things about Enchanting in Minecraft, yet some remain the same. "
				""
				"Enchanting tables will only detect blocks modifying it's stats if they're exactly one block away from the table just like in Vanilla, These stats however alter the behaviour fo your enchantments."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&a&nEterna&r&r, also known as  Enchanting Power, determines the level of your enchantments. Different tiers and types of bookshelves will add varying amounts. Beware every type of shelf has a maximum capacity of &a&nEterna&r&r beyond which it will no longer contribute to the value."
				""
				"The level of your enchantment is 2x your Eterna value. If you reach the maximum of 50 &n&aEterna&r&r you will be enchanting at level 100."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&n&4Quanta&r&r refers to the instability of your enchantments. A short description would be Enchanting Flux. This can be both a good and a bad thing as it can both increase or decrease the true level of enchantment that will be applied. "
				""
				"The amount it increases or decreases depends on the enchanting table's Quanta value. If the table has a Quanta value of 50, the actual enchantment value can be -50 or +50."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&n&5Arcana&r&r is the value that determines the availability of rare enchants. These are often more powerful enchantments that will give the item a powerful boon. The higher the value the easier it is to get rare enchants on whatever it is you're enchanting. "
				""
				"However very high levels of &5&nArcana&r&r will also make common enchantments more difficult to get."
			]
			id: "2172A6251E7C57A8"
			rewards: [
				{
					exclude_from_claim_all: true
					id: "299E61F0BA970F83"
					table_id: 8678092705658131358L
					type: "choice"
				}
				{
					id: "6931E7D726999DAB"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 2
				}
				{
					count: 10
					id: "08F6E0B772C8A4BA"
					item: "minecraft:bookshelf"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "Enchanting Properties"
			tasks: [{
				id: "62E466E5012D5CCC"
				item: "minecraft:enchanting_table"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2172A6251E7C57A8"]
			description: [
				"&n&eRectification&r&r is a modifier that interacts with &4&nQuanta&r&r."
				""
				"The way it interacts is by stripping away the negative scalar of the Enchanting Flux. &n&4Quanta&r&r can both increase and decrease the applied level of enchantments, the higher the rectification the smaller the negative value. At 100% &n&eRectification&r&r, enchantments will no longer be able to go lower, the &n&4Quanta&r&r instability can only improve their level."
			]
			icon: "apotheosis:rectifier"
			id: "722D72A914A3A75B"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 8
					id: "436B22DE5D260776"
